<newsitem itemid="210966" id="root" date="1996-11-22" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Hyder H1 pretax profit rises.</title>
<headline>Hyder H1 pretax profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending Sept 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		57.7		   vs 57.4</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 14.6		   vs 12.6</p>
<p> Pretax		     100.7		  vs 80.6</p>
<p> Turnover		   547.7		  vs 269.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 96 to 109 million stg.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 133.2		  vs 83.3</p>
<p> Interest receivable    11.6		   vs 15.5</p>
<p> Interest payable	 46.1		   vs 18.7</p>
<p> Tax			  10.9		   vs 8.5</p>
<p> Net taxed		  89.8		   vs 72.1</p>
<p> Attributable	     81.5		   vs 70.3</p>
<p> Pay date		   March 3, 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  Dec 17</p>
<p> Ex-div date		Dec 9</p>
<p>NOTE: Hyder Plc was formed when Welsh Water took over regional electricity company South Wales Electricity (Swalec) at the start of the year.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
